# Deterministic Gates

Structural gates live in `.specs/harness/scripts/` and require Python 3. A non-zero exit means STOP.

| When | Command |
| --- | --- |
| Before confirming a spec | `python3 .specs/harness/scripts/validate_spec.py [feature]` |
| Before approving tasks | `python3 .specs/harness/scripts/validate_tasks.py [feature]` |
| On each commit | `python3 .specs/harness/scripts/check_commit.py --message "<message>"` |
| Before declaring done | `python3 .specs/harness/scripts/validate_state.py [feature]` |

Gates accept a feature name, a feature directory, or a path to the artifact. With no argument they auto-detect when the project has exactly one feature.

If Python is unavailable, perform the same checks by reading the artifact against the reference checklist.

Persistent state: `.specs/STATE.md` (decisions/handoff), `.specs/lessons.json` (canonical lessons), `.specs/LESSONS.md` (generated playbook). Commit `.specs/` via `/handoff` — see `git-handoff.md`.
